{"name":"Flying Carpet","hex":"#787489","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flying carpet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A carpet capable either of magical flight, or instantaneous transport from one place to another, used as a means of travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flying_carpet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flying Carpet (game)","blocks":[{"text":"Flying Carpet is a board game published by Ravensburger in 1987."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flying_Carpet_(game)"},{"title":"Magic carpet","blocks":[{"text":"A magic carpet, also called a flying carpet, is a legendary carpet and common trope in fantasy fiction. It is typically used as a form of transportation and can quickly or instantaneously carry its user(s) to their destination."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Vasnetsov_samolet.jpg/330px-Vasnetsov_samolet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_carpet"},{"title":"Carpet","blocks":[{"text":"A carpet or rug is a textile floor covering that typically consists of an upper layer of pile attached to a backing. In Europe, the pile was traditionally made of wool, but since the 20th century, synthetic fibres such as polypropylene, nylon, and polyester have been used as less expensive alternatives. The pile often consists of twisted tufts that are heat-treated to maintain their structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Wollteppich_1.jpg/330px-Wollteppich_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Stamp_IQ_1966_50f.jpg/120px-Stamp_IQ_1966_50f.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Stamp_IQ_1966_50f.jpg/250px-S